description:
Read ARCHITECTURE §3, §5 (all of it), §6, §12, §13, and API.md §1-4 and §15.

Setup: `sdk: ^3.13.0`. Add the deps of ARCH 2.1 with `dart pub add`, including http_parser, async and dev fake_async. Commit pubspec.lock. Dockerfile exactly as ARCH 5.20 (`mkdir -p /out`, USER 64090).

CLI (bin/server.dart): serve, hash-password, healthcheck, check-config (reports sources, admin user id auto/set, PBKDF2 timing), reset-admin. Set umask 077 at start.

Config (5.2): non-secret env plus the secrets file YAMS_HUB_SECRETS_FILE (KEY='value' parser). The bootstrap hash is ignored once users.json exists. CORS origin validation. HOST_SYS=/sys, HOST_NET_DEV, SHELFMARK_URL, JELLYFIN_ADMIN_USER_ID auto-detect. Policy YAML including adminRefreshTokenTtlDays and imageCache limits.

Pipeline (5.3): requestId, hostCheck (ping exempt), accessLog, securityHeaders/CSP/CORP, cors, errorHandler (messages redacted). ApiRouter mounted at both /api/v1 and /yh/api/v1 with `Router(notFoundHandler: jsonNotFound)`, regex-constrained params, static-before-param registration.

Auth (5.4):
- users and sessions stores (0600);
- PBKDF2 with fail-closed parsing, auto-tune and a global semaphore (2 running, 8 queued, else 429);
- access tokens indexed by session;
- self-identifying refresh tokens with reuse revocation;
- per-session server proof (login serverProofKey; `/ping?nonce&sid` proof);
- cookie transport on /yh with the cookie paths given there, CSRF header on all cookie requests except img GETs and on cookie login, Secure only on HTTPS;
- limiter counts attempts before hashing, known-IP exemption, bridge-IP skip;
- the invalidation table; authenticate() reads role/disabled from the store per request.

FeatureModule/FeatureContext (5.5) with every member listed: config, upstreams, caches, pollers, jobs, audit, images, remoteHttp (RemoteFetcher), jellyfin (JellyfinServerInfo), seerrIdentity, seerrSettings, health, stores, redact, clock, log.

Upstreams (5.6): UpstreamClient with absolute paths incl. API prefix, multipart, maxBytes, auth strategies (shelfmark none), QbitSession, DockerClient prepending /v1.54, error mapping, transport exceptions rethrown without text. RemoteFetcher: manual redirects, public-IP check, magnet redirect.

Rest of core:
- caches/pollers (5.7); watchtowerCheck probe via GET /v1/containers/details (never /v1/check);
- ImageUrls with the exact signatures of 5.8, and ImageRoutes with validation, buckets, raster magic-byte sniffing, SVG ban, headers, streaming cap, growth control, Seerr avatar host assertion, gravatar allow-list;
- JobRegistry and /jobs (member filter, redacted logs);
- HealthService and /health (incl. shelfmark GET /api/health), plus the docker proxy self-test that disables container actions;
- dashboard aggregation (stubs throw notImplemented); audit with sanitize (5.13); redactSecrets (5.14); static handler (5.15).

Core routes: /ping, /auth/**, /admin/** (incl. POST /admin/jellyfin-users/{id}/import-to-seerr), /server, /health, /jobs, /img/**, /dashboard.

creates_stubs (create once, never touch again): gateway/lib/src/features/{requests,library,activity,calendar,indexers,subtitles,containers,system,media}/<id>_module.dart. Each registers EVERY API.md route of its feature (regex params, static first) returning 501, and its dashboard() throws ApiException.notImplemented(). Also core/feature_registry.dart.

Test support (5.19): TestHub(startModules: false, startOnly, FakeClock), fake_upstreams on MockClient.streaming with call recording, fixture() loader.

Core tests: everything in 5.19's core list, including the stub-path 501 test, upstream path assertions, ImageUrls round trips and the check-config secrets-file test.

Acceptance: dart analyze clean, tests green, docker build smoke passes.
